1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,724
Here's a quest, in the crew's Quest Log,

2
00:00:03,174 --> 00:00:07,231
and here's a boss, chosen on the server before the game starts.

3
00:00:08,131 --> 00:00:10,961
Here's a boarding party, on a crew member's handheld,

4
00:00:11,411 --> 00:00:13,873
and here's an ancient ruin, on the main screen.

5
00:00:14,773 --> 00:00:19,279
A writer typed every one of these, in plain words, in a text file.

6
00:00:20,179 --> 00:00:23,812
And by the end of this course, that writer is you.

7
00:00:25,612 --> 00:00:28,362
Today, you don't type anything at all.

8
00:00:29,262 --> 00:00:31,432
You play, and you watch,

9
00:00:31,882 --> 00:00:33,783
and I show you what you're going to build.

10
00:00:34,983 --> 00:00:37,183
Artemis Cosmos is a starship bridge.

11
00:00:38,083 --> 00:00:42,241
One copy of the game runs the story, and we call that the server.

12
00:00:43,141 --> 00:00:44,965
Every other screen is one station:

13
00:00:45,415 --> 00:00:48,985
Helm steers, Weapons fires, Science scans,

14
00:00:49,435 --> 00:00:52,565
Comms talks, and Engineering keeps her running.

15
00:00:54,365 --> 00:00:58,156
What the crew is asked to do, who calls them, and what they find:

16
00:00:58,606 --> 00:01:00,007
all of that is a mission.

17
00:01:00,907 --> 00:01:02,615
And a mission is what you'll write.

18
00:01:03,815 --> 00:01:05,008
Start the game with me.

19
00:01:05,908 --> 00:01:07,678
The first screen has the game's name,

20
00:01:08,128 --> 00:01:13,317
and three buttons at the bottom left: start server, start client, and options.

21
00:01:14,217 --> 00:01:18,051
One computer runs the game for everybody, so press start server.

22
00:01:19,851 --> 00:01:21,396
Now you make two choices here.

23
00:01:22,296 --> 00:01:26,188
First, you choose a mission, and that's Legendary Missions.

24
00:01:26,638 --> 00:01:30,320
Press initialize mission, and wait a few seconds.

25
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:34,440
Then you choose a map inside it, and that's Siege.

26
00:01:36,240 --> 00:01:38,222
Remember both of those lists,

27
00:01:38,672 --> 00:01:42,500
because in two lectures' time, there's a line in the first one that you made.

28
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:46,107
Now press the start mission button.

29
00:01:47,007 --> 00:01:48,987
The server only runs the game,

30
00:01:49,437 --> 00:01:54,447
so to fly, you start the game a second time, and press start client.

31
00:01:55,348 --> 00:01:58,455
Connect to your own server, pick Helm, and press ready.

32
00:01:59,655 --> 00:02:02,406
This is the Quest Log, on the crew's handheld,

33
00:02:02,856 --> 00:02:05,670
and under Game is what the game has asked us to do.

34
00:02:06,570 --> 00:02:08,453
It's one job, in three parts:

35
00:02:08,903 --> 00:02:13,312
break the siege, don't lose every starbase, and mind the clock.

36
00:02:15,112 --> 00:02:17,977
Now look at this, because this is the file.

37
00:02:18,877 --> 00:02:23,233
The square brackets hold the name on that Quest Log line,

38
00:02:23,683 --> 00:02:26,766
and the last line is the words the crew reads,

39
00:02:27,216 --> 00:02:28,606
when they select that line.

40
00:02:29,506 --> 00:02:32,406
Required, true, means you can't win without it.

41
00:02:34,206 --> 00:02:37,568
Nobody programmed this quest. Somebody typed it.

42
00:02:38,468 --> 00:02:42,205
And Class One ends with you having typed a chain of these.

43
00:02:43,405 --> 00:02:45,643
Now the same map, with one change.

44
00:02:46,543 --> 00:02:51,071
On the server's start screen, the options panel has a line called Boss,

45
00:02:51,521 --> 00:02:53,096
and I choose the Warlord.

46
00:02:54,896 --> 00:02:56,459
A boss doesn't come at the start.

47
00:02:57,359 --> 00:03:00,929
She waits until we've destroyed three raiders in every four.

48
00:03:01,829 --> 00:03:04,884
Then she arrives, and a new job joins the Quest Log.

49
00:03:06,684 --> 00:03:09,163
Now here's her file, the one that makes her.

50
00:03:10,063 --> 00:03:12,663
Twenty-five percent means a quarter are left.

51
00:03:13,113 --> 00:03:16,224
Then two fleets, and her name and her hull.

52
00:03:17,124 --> 00:03:21,599
In Class Two, you copy this file, change the words,

53
00:03:22,049 --> 00:03:24,776
and your own boss is in that list.

54
00:03:25,976 --> 00:03:28,056
This one, you can't play today.

55
00:03:28,956 --> 00:03:32,110
It isn't in the game's menus, so just watch.

56
00:03:33,910 --> 00:03:36,181
Some of the crew leave the ship,

57
00:03:36,631 --> 00:03:38,758
and each console becomes a handheld.

58
00:03:39,658 --> 00:03:42,583
There's a line of story, and the ways out, as buttons.

59
00:03:44,383 --> 00:03:46,012
Now think of two of them together.

60
00:03:46,912 --> 00:03:49,335
They're in the same room, with different choices:

61
00:03:49,785 --> 00:03:52,204
the surgeon is offered what the engineer isn't.

62
00:03:53,104 --> 00:03:56,947
It's a story told in rooms, and every reader has their own copy.

63
00:03:57,397 --> 00:03:59,109
And that's what Class Three teaches.

64
00:04:00,309 --> 00:04:03,604
And then there's this, a ruin called The Voice,

65
00:04:04,054 --> 00:04:07,849
from Storm's Beacon, a mission that's still being made.

66
00:04:08,748 --> 00:04:10,986
This is the main screen as we arrive,

67
00:04:11,436 --> 00:04:15,050
and that's the station ahead, dark for a thousand years.

68
00:04:16,850 --> 00:04:19,065
Helm takes us in through a docking throat,

69
00:04:19,515 --> 00:04:23,230
and inside, it's rooms with flat walls and real corners.

70
00:04:24,130 --> 00:04:26,981
Close to the way in, the handheld offers suit up,

71
00:04:27,431 --> 00:04:30,140
so some of the crew can fly the halls in suits.

72
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:34,642
In the file, every room is one record,

73
00:04:35,092 --> 00:04:38,013
and its box line says where it is, and how big.

74
00:04:38,913 --> 00:04:41,012
This line picks what the walls are made of,

75
00:04:41,462 --> 00:04:43,563
and the game lays them for you.

76
00:04:45,363 --> 00:04:48,295
Storm's Beacon isn't out yet, so you can't play this one.

77
00:04:49,195 --> 00:04:51,813
But in Class Four, you build a ruin like it.

78
00:04:53,013 --> 00:04:54,142
So what is a mission?

79
00:04:55,042 --> 00:04:56,925
It's a folder, with seven files,

80
00:04:57,375 --> 00:04:59,281
and five of them are made for you.

81
00:05:00,181 --> 00:05:03,911
The two that matter are the fact sheet, and the story file.

82
00:05:05,711 --> 00:05:08,348
The fact sheet is every word the crew reads.

83
00:05:09,248 --> 00:05:12,445
Here's one quest from Class One's mission, in the Quest Log:

84
00:05:12,895 --> 00:05:16,260
Close Inspection, and what the crew is told about it.

85
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:19,831
When we fly within five hundred of the hulk,

86
00:05:20,281 --> 00:05:22,149
the Quest Log marks it done.

87
00:05:23,949 --> 00:05:25,980
And here it is in the fact sheet:

88
00:05:26,430 --> 00:05:30,060
its name, its facts between the two rows of hyphens,

89
00:05:30,510 --> 00:05:32,246
and what the crew is told.

90
00:05:33,146 --> 00:05:35,930
Done when, reach derelict five hundred.

91
00:05:36,380 --> 00:05:38,251
It means just what it says.

92
00:05:40,051 --> 00:05:43,604
The story file is short, and it comes ready-made.

93
00:05:44,504 --> 00:05:48,770
On Helm, twenty seconds after the crew is told to wait for a tug,

94
00:05:49,220 --> 00:05:51,459
the game says the tug has arrived.

95
00:05:52,359 --> 00:05:56,092
It comes from a card, pasted into the story file, like this one.

96
00:05:56,992 --> 00:06:00,297
It says: when the step starts, wait twenty seconds,

97
00:06:00,747 --> 00:06:02,836
bring in a tug, and tell the quests.

98
00:06:04,636 --> 00:06:06,708
You'll be able to read this by Lecture Eleven.

99
00:06:07,608 --> 00:06:09,868
And you'll never write one from a blank page.

100
00:06:11,068 --> 00:06:12,835
There are six classes in all.

101
00:06:13,735 --> 00:06:16,923
One is your desk, and a story told in quests.

102
00:06:17,373 --> 00:06:20,750
Two is people who talk, and a boss of your own.

103
00:06:21,650 --> 00:06:24,632
Then come three that you can take in any order:

104
00:06:25,082 --> 00:06:28,399
three is boarding parties, four is ruins,

105
00:06:28,849 --> 00:06:31,618
and five is a universe of your own.

106
00:06:32,518 --> 00:06:36,291
And six is twenty evenings of play in that universe.

107
00:06:38,091 --> 00:06:42,747
Some of the later lectures are still being made, and the page says which.

108
00:06:43,947 --> 00:06:46,028
So play ten minutes of Siege.

109
00:06:46,928 --> 00:06:48,897
Write down three things that happened,

110
00:06:49,347 --> 00:06:51,776
and who, or what, caused each one.

111
00:06:52,676 --> 00:06:54,084
And keep the page you write,

112
00:06:54,534 --> 00:06:58,815
because next time, we find where all of this lives on your computer.
